<body>
<h1>Standard Operating Procedure (SOP) for Network Configuration</h1>
<p>This SOP outlines the steps for configuring a network environment in ServiceNow.</p>

<h2>Purpose</h2>
<p>The purpose of this SOP is to provide a standardized process for configuring networks in ServiceNow, ensuring consistency and efficiency across the organization.</p>

<h2>Scope</h2>
<ul>
  <li>Applicable to all IT teams using ServiceNow for network configuration</li>
  <li>Scope includes network devices, such as routers, switches, and firewalls</li>
  <li>Scope does not include infrastructure or hardware maintenance</li>
</ul>

<h2>Prerequisites</h2>
<ul>
  <li>ServiceNow instance with the required network configuration tools</li>
  <li>Network device credentials (username and password)</li>
  <li>Basic understanding of network concepts and terminology</li>
</ul>

<h2>Roles and Responsibilities</h2>
<table border="1" cellpadding="6" cellspacing="0">
  <thead><tr><th>Role</th><th>Responsibility</th></tr></thead>
  <tbody>
    <tr><td>Network Administrator</td><td>Configure network devices, monitor network activity, and troubleshoot issues.</td></tr>
    <tr><td>IT Team Members</td><td>Assist in configuring network devices, report on network performance, and request support for troubleshooting issues.</td></tr>
  </tbody>
</table>

<h2>Procedure</h2>
<ol>
  <li>Log in to the ServiceNow instance and navigate to the Network Configuration tool.</li>
  <li>Select the device to be configured from the list of available devices.</li>
  <li>Enter the network device credentials (username and password) to access the device's configuration interface.</li>
  <li>Configure the device according to the organization's established network policies and procedures.</li>
  <li>Save changes and update the Network Configuration tool.</li>
</ol>

<h2>Required Screenshot / Image</h2>
<div style="border:1px solid #999;padding:16px;background:#f5f5f5;">
  <strong>Image Placeholder:</strong> The generated image will be inserted here after ServiceNow attachment upload.
</div>

<h2>Validation</h2>
<ul>
  <li>Verify that the device is configured correctly and functioning as expected.</li>
  <li>Check for any errors or warnings in the Network Configuration tool.</li>
  <li>Validate that network connectivity and performance meet the organization's standards.</li>
</ul>

<h2>Troubleshooting</h2>
<table border="1" cellpadding="6" cellspacing="0">
  <thead><tr><th>Issue</th><th>Cause</th><th>Resolution</th></tr></thead>
  <tbody>
    <tr><td>Device not responding to configuration changes.</td><td>Cause: Incorrect credentials or device configuration issues.</td><td>Resolution: Check credentials, verify device configuration, and try again.</td></tr>
    <tr><td>Network connectivity issues.</td><td>Cause: Incorrect IP address or subnet mask configuration.</td><td>Resolution: Review IP address and subnet mask settings, and update as necessary.</td></tr>
  </tbody>
</table>

<h2>Rollback / Recovery</h2>
<ol>
  <li>If a network issue arises, verify the device's current configuration and check for any errors in the Network Configuration tool.</li>
  <li>Roll back to the previous configuration by selecting the "Previous" button in the Network Configuration tool.</li>
  <li>If necessary, contact the IT team or management for further assistance or guidance.</li>
</ol>

<h2>References</h2>
<ul>
  <li>ServiceNow documentation on network configuration</li>
  <li>Organization's established network policies and procedures</li>
  <li>NICI (Network Configuration Interface) user guide</li>
</ul>
</body>
</html>
